# P09.28 — Phase 2b.2: `swift_value!` macro auto-synthesizes
# Drop + Clone for `#[repr(swift)]` value types and classes.
#
# Workspace-only. No compiler changes.
#
# # Before / after
#
# Before: every `#[repr(swift)]` binding needs a manual metadata
# extern + `impl Drop` + `impl Clone` — a ~30-line boilerplate
# chunk per type (see `/tmp/p09-swift-nt/src/lib.rs` or the
# outdated HTML §11 example).
#
# After:
#
# ```rust
# rustcc_macros::swift_value! {
#     #[rustc_swift_type = "MyLib.NT"]
#     pub struct NT {
#         pub x: u64,
#         pub inner: *mut core::ffi::c_void,
#     }
# }
# ```
#
# That's it — the macro emits `#[repr(swift)]`, the metadata
# accessor `extern "C"` declaration with the Itanium / Swift
# mangling (`$s<mod><type>VMa` for values, `$s<mod><type>CMa`
# for classes), and fully wired `impl Drop` + `impl Clone`
# forwarding to `rustcc_swift_rt::{drop_swift_value,
# clone_swift_value}` (values) or
# `{release_swift_class, retain_swift_class}` (classes).
#
# # Design choice — macro, not compiler synthesis
#
# The queue state originally called Phase 2b.2 "compiler
# auto-synthesis". That path would require emitting synthetic
# HIR nodes for trait impls — a pattern the fork hasn't used and
# would need a meaningful design + risk review. The macro
# approach delivers the same user-facing ergonomic win in
# ~200 LOC, is isolated to `rustcc_macros`, and matches the
# precedent set by P09.22's `cxx_class_native!`.
#
# The compiler-synthesis path is still documented as a future
# cleanup: it'd let users drop the `swift_value!` wrapper
# entirely and tag the struct directly.
#
# # Scope (v1)
#
# - ASCII module and type names only. Non-ASCII (operators,
#   non-Latin-script) would need Swift's full mangling (punycode
#   / operator-name runs). Failing parse returns a compile-time
#   error from the macro.
# - Non-generic types only. Generic Swift types have richer
#   metadata accessor shapes.
# - Class-backed bindings assume a single-field struct with the
#   class pointer at offset 0. Multi-field class wrappers would
#   need per-field Clone logic.
# - Metadata accessor signature assumed to be
#   `fn(usize) -> MetadataResponse`. Matches every case seen on
#   x86_64-apple-darwin / aarch64-apple-darwin.
#
# # Validation
#
# - `/tmp/p09-28-swift-auto/` — full probe. Types:
#   `#[rustc_swift_type = "MyLib.NT"]` value type with a class
#   field (`inner: *mut c_void`). Exercises the auto-emitted
#   Clone + Drop observing `inner_deinit_count` between steps:
#
#   ```
#   after make_nt: deinit=0 (want 0)
#   after clone  : deinit=0 (want 0)   # auto Clone -> retain
#   after drop(b): deinit=0 (want 0)   # auto Drop  -> release (refcount 1)
#   after drop(a): deinit=1 (want 1)   # auto Drop  -> release (refcount 0 -> deinit)
#   OK, exit 0
#   ```
#
# - `cargo test --workspace` → 235/0 preserved.
#
# # Files
#
# - `crates/rustcc_macros/src/lib.rs` — `swift_value!` proc
#   macro (~200 lines added).
#
# No compiler changes.

diff --git a/crates/rustcc_macros/src/lib.rs b/crates/rustcc_macros/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/rustcc_macros/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/rustcc_macros/src/lib.rs
@@ (imports — extend)
 use syn::{
     parse::{Parse, ParseStream},
     parse_macro_input,
-    FnArg, Ident, Item, LitInt, Pat, PatType, ReturnType, Signature, Token,
-    Type, TypePath, TypePtr, TypeReference, Visibility,
+    Attribute, Expr, ExprLit, FnArg, Ident, Item, ItemStruct, Lit, LitInt,
+    LitStr, Meta, Pat, PatType, ReturnType, Signature, Token, Type, TypePath,
+    TypePtr, TypeReference, Visibility,
 };

@@ (end of file — new section)
